#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File:         pp_build_exe.args
#
# Description:  Arguments for building a stand-alone Windows executable for
#               the ExifTool Metadata Stripper (strip_tool/).
#
#               This is deliberately a much shorter dependency list than the
#               main exiftool.exe build (see ../pp_build_exe.args) -- this
#               tool only ever reads a file's metadata and deletes it, so it
#               doesn't need the CSV/JSON import, hashing, archive-format, or
#               geotagging support that the full command-line application
#               pulls in.
#
# Requires:     PAR::Packer (provides the "pp" command) and Perl/Tk,
#               installed under the same Perl that will run this command.
#               On Windows:  cpan install PAR::Packer Tk
#
# Build:        Don't run this file directly -- run build.bat in this
#               directory instead (double-click it, or type ".\build.bat"
#               from PowerShell/cmd). This file just holds the pp arguments
#               build.bat passes through.
#
# Why -x:       Perl/Tk loads its widget classes (Frame, Button, Listbox,
#               etc.) on demand via AUTOLOAD rather than a static "use", so
#               pp's static scanner can't see them by itself, and the exact
#               set of internal modules behind things like getOpenFile/
#               chooseDirectory differs between Windows and X11 builds of
#               Tk. Rather than hand-guess that list and risk it being
#               wrong on your particular Tk build, this uses pp's "-x" flag
#               (the officially documented fix for exactly this problem),
#               which runs the app live during packaging and records
#               whatever it actually loads. That's why build.bat pops the
#               app up during the build -- click through it once (see the
#               on-screen instructions) and the build finishes on its own.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-x
-o ExifMetadataStripper.exe
-I ../lib
-I lib
-M ExifStripper::Core
-M Encode
-M Compress::Zlib
-M Time::HiRes
-M Win32::API
-M Win32API::File
-M Tk
-M Tk::Font
exif_metadata_stripper.pl
# end
